     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · ESPN Cricinfo · 2026-11-09 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Cricket Scotland Limits Fixtures with Afghanistan</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Scotland</span> <span>#Afghanistan</span> <span>#ICC</span></div>
       <p>Cricket Scotland has announced a significant reduction in its cricketing relations with Afghanistan, a move that will reshape future bilateral engagements. This decision was formally communicated by the Scottish cricketing body, as detailed by ESPN Cricinfo.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/cricket-scotland-limits-fixtures-with-afghanistan.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Henceforth, Scotland's teams will restrict their competitive encounters with Afghanistan solely to International Cricket Council (ICC) events. This policy means that all other forms of bilateral competition, including tours or standalone matches, will cease.</p><p>The change stems from an in-depth review undertaken by Cricket Scotland's board. This review specifically assessed the nature of the countries' engagement, leading to the strategic decision to scale back interactions.</p><p>What to watch: Future implications for bilateral cricket scheduling and international relations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a concise and accurate summary of the provided information regarding Cricket Scotland's policy shift.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1562059.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
