       <h1>Embraer Targets India for C-390 Export Hub</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Embraer</span> <span>#C-390</span></div>
       <p>Brazilian aerospace firm Embraer is reportedly eyeing the Indian Air Force's (IAF) 60-plane Medium Transport Aircraft (MTA) deal. This initiative specifically involves the C-390 aircraft, according to a report from Defence.in.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/embraer-targets-india-for-c-390-export-hub.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The company's strategic vision extends beyond the immediate procurement, aiming to establish India as a crucial export hub for the C-390. This would leverage India's industrial base for broader regional distribution.</p><p>The broader Asian market presents a substantial opportunity, with Defence.in indicating a potential demand for up to 500 such jets. The IAF's 60-plane order is seen as a foundational step for Embraer in tapping into this extensive market.</p><p>What to watch: Progress on the IAF's MTA tender and Embraer's proposal.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the core details of Embraer's strategy regarding the IAF tender and the broader Asian market potential.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiygFBVV95cUxQU1VnZGR2WnZicmJXNnVBUzQyWEgzNnAxNUlNQXR0THpSd2VKVjU0QzllTmMzRDJsY3NsTDFPT2R2c2NDSmNpZ2pZZ01od2p5TDhwV3B2Q3dLQUN4Vlh3UlREZzFWQzVqRlMwclZOMm53ZjBZbDRBYTEyeV8xSVMxNzNZcWJwUVVzQ0tFRFZRSUdZNnEzTnZYMW16WENRelV1RjJVMTBuTmZfQ28tTjhvQXlHSVVwMzExY3h3bHhMWndNYV94b1JrY2Zn?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
