       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-11-09 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>England Defeats Australia 45-22 in Nations Championship</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>England secured a dominant 45-22 victory over Australia in the Nations Championship, marking their highest-ever points tally against the Wallabies. Coach Steve Borthwick’s side displayed improved intensity, discipline, and tactical accuracy, effectively countering expectations of a stern Australian challenge. The performance represents a significant step forward from England's Six Nations and summer tour results.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/england-defeats-australia-45-22-in-nations-championship.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>England's backline, featuring George Furbank, Tommy Freeman, and Immanuel Feyi-Waboso, proved particularly disruptive. Analyst Matt Dawson noted that the team appeared galvanized following reports of internal leadership friction. The win provides a positive start to the autumn series, with observers highlighting the controlled decision-making and well-drilled nature of the current squad.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the match outcome and the analyst's commentary within the target length.</p>
