       <h1>ESPN Secures Rights to Expanded College Football Playoff</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Disney-owned media giant ESPN has finalized a new deal to become the exclusive worldwide rightsholder for an expanded 24-team College Football Playoff. This agreement solidifies the network's position as a primary broadcaster for high-level collegiate sports.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/espn-secures-rights-to-expanded-college-football-playoff.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The expansion reflects a broader trend in the media industry, where demand for premium live sports content remains exceptionally high. By capturing the rights to this larger playoff structure, ESPN aims to capitalize on the sustained popularity of college football, ensuring it remains the central platform for viewers following the tournament's evolution into a 24-team format.</p>
