     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · BBC World · 2026-11-09 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by BBC World, Al Jazeera">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>France Blames Iran for Supermarket Fridge Cyber-Attacks</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>France has formally accused Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps of orchestrating cyber-attacks that disabled supermarket refrigeration systems. The breach caused widespread food spoilage, resulting in millions of euros in damages across the country. French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot described the aggression as unprecedented and confirmed plans to implement European-level sanctions against those responsible.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/france-blames-iran-for-supermarket-fridge-cyber-attacks.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Separately, the Paris prosecutor has launched an investigation into the head of an Iranian offensive cyber unit. Recent reports indicate that supermarkets in seven additional European nations have also faced similar attacks. Iran has not yet issued a response to these allegations regarding the ongoing digital targeting of European grocery infrastructure.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and captures the essential details provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source · also covered by 1 more</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmg474vk6dyqo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC World</a></li><li><a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/9/france-accuses-iran-of-cyberattack-on-european-fridges?traffic_source=rss" rel="noopener">Al Jazeera</a></li></ul>
      <p>This brief was written from the original report. The same event was independently covered by the other outlets listed here.</p>
    </div>
       
