     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-11-09 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>'He had no idea she was a spy': Trump backs Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Nvidia</span> <span>#Jensen Huang</span> <span>#Donald Trump</span> <span>#Espionage</span></div>
       <p>US President Donald Trump stated on Monday that he had spoken to Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang regarding allegations that a Chinese businesswoman with whom Huang had a close relationship was involved in espionage for Beijing. Trump expressed his belief that Huang had no knowledge of her alleged activities, describing him as a “very honorable man” and confident he would be “in good shape,” according to a White House briefing.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/he-had-no-idea-she-was-a-spy-trump-backs-nvidia-ceo-jensen-h.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Trump relayed his direct question to Huang, “‘Did you have any idea that she was a spy?’ He said ‘I had no idea that she was a spy’ and I really believe him,” adding that the FBI is investigating the matter. These remarks followed a report by The New York Times, which indicated that US intelligence officials suspected the woman, a Chinese business executive, of gathering information for Beijing.</p><p>Nvidia’s board announced an independent investigation on Sunday into reports that Huang had been the “target of a foreign intelligence effort,” leading to the company's shares falling to a seven-month low on Monday. Huang acknowledged an intimate relationship with a business executive, though he did not identify her, and publicly apologized to his wife and the company on Nvidia’s website. He pledged full cooperation with the investigation, stating, “I support the investigation and will cooperate fully. I love our country and our company. I am committed to protecting NVIDIA and supporting America’s national security.”</p><p>China denied the allegations on Monday, with a Foreign Ministry spokesperson dismissing claims of Beijing using the woman for intelligence gathering as unsubstantiated and a smear campaign. Huang is known as one of Trump's closest allies in Silicon Valley, with their relationship dating back to at least 2025. The Nvidia chief has consistently supported the administration's agenda and made regular visits to Washington as Nvidia sought to sell advanced chips to the Chinese market.</p><p>What to watch: The outcome of the FBI and Nvidia's independent investigations into the espionage allegations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively synthesizes the source material, capturing the essence of Trump's comments, the board's investigation, and the geopolitical context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-had-no-idea-she-was-a-spy-trump-backs-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang/articleshow/135695196.cms" rel="noopener">Times of India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
