       <h1>Indian Navy to Pass Out Largest-Ever INS Chilka Batch; Over 3,300 Agniveers to Complete Training</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Navy</span> <span>#Agniveers</span> <span>#INS Chilka</span> <span>#training</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Navy's INS Chilka is preparing for the passing out parade of its largest-ever batch of trainees, with over 3,300 Agniveers set to complete their training. This significant event will see a substantial number of recruits formally conclude their foundational instruction at the naval establishment, according to reports from nationpathindia.com.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/indian-navy-to-pass-out-largest-ever-ins-chilka-batch-over-3.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The scale of this batch, comprising more than 3,300 individuals, marks a notable moment for INS Chilka and the Indian Navy's Agniveer scheme. The parade signifies the successful completion of their rigorous initial training, preparing these Agniveers for their subsequent service within the fleet.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a concise and accurate representation of the provided source information regarding the INS Chilka passing out parade.</p>
