     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-11-09 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>IOA Leadership Battle Intensifies with Usha, Saina in SOM Elections</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Sports</span> <span>#Olympics</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Olympic Association's (IOA) electoral battle enters a crucial phase on Monday, with current president PT Usha facing a test in the Sportspersons of Outstanding Merit (SOM) elections. Olympic medallist Saina Nehwal is also a contender, amidst speculation of a leadership challenge to Usha. The election for four women's SOM positions is significant as Nehwal's name emerged as a potential challenger to Usha in the December 5 elections for the IOA Executive Council, which will elect the next president.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/ioa-leadership-battle-intensifies-with-usha-saina-in-som-ele.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Usha and Nehwal are not directly contesting for the president's post on Monday. They are among six candidates for four women's SOM positions, with their performance potentially crucial for the subsequent leadership contest. The other four women candidates are former long jumper Anju Bobby George, former archer Dola Banerjee, former Indian women's hockey captain Rani Rampal, and former basketball player Anitha Paul Durai. In the men's category, four candidates were elected unopposed: Olympic medallists Gagan Narang, Yogeshwar Dutt, Vijender Singh, and former table tennis player Kamlesh Mehta, after eight of 12 contenders withdrew.</p><p>The women's category is the only contested segment of the SOM elections, with four positions among six candidates, following five withdrawals before the November 7 deadline. These elections are vital for the wider IOA electoral process for the 2026-2030 term. Elected representatives join the IOA General Assembly, becoming eligible to vote and contest in the December 5 elections for the new Executive Council. One male and one female SOM representative will also secure Executive Council places, gaining a direct governing role.</p><p>Usha, the first woman IOA president elected in December 2022, seeks to retain her position amidst this emerging contest. Saina, a 2012 London Olympics bronze medallist, is a prominent name linked to the possible leadership contest, though her presidential candidature is not formally established. Electoral Officer Sanjay Kumar Srivastava oversees the process, with virtual voting for women's SOM positions scheduled for Monday. The December 5 election will determine the IOA's next Executive Council, leading the Olympic movement for 2026-2030, as India pursues hosting the 2036 Olympic Games.</p><p>What to watch: The outcome of Monday's virtual SOM elections and the formal nominations for the December 5 presidential contest.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft captures all key details of the IOA electoral process, including the specific candidates and the significance of the SOM elections.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/othersports/ioa-leadership-battle-gathers-pace-as-usha-saina-feature-in-crucial-som-elections-12302128#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
