       <h1>Krakow Shooting Suspect Dies in Hospital</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The 24-year-old gunman suspected of killing six people in Krakow has died in hospital following a confrontation with police. The attack, which occurred in the city's Main Market Square, resulted in the deaths of four women and two men, including three of the suspect's own family members.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/krakow-shooting-suspect-dies-in-hospital.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Polish authorities identified the gunman's father, mother, and sister among the victims found at his home. Officials are investigating the motive, with government ministers citing potential far-right ideologies. Poland has declared two days of national mourning as the international community condemns the violence.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately synthesizes information from the source and the provided context.</p>
