     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-09 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Muslim Youth League Leaders Booked Over Kochi Rally</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Police in Kochi have registered a case against 12 Muslim Youth League (MYL) leaders, including State president Sayyid Munavvar Ali Shihab Thangal and MLA Fathima Thahiliya. The charges follow a rally from Bolgatty to the Kerala High Court Junction that allegedly caused significant traffic obstruction.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/muslim-youth-league-leaders-booked-over-kochi-rally.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The FIR states that approximately 2,000 participants blocked vehicular and pedestrian movement along Shanmukham Road on Sunday. The case was filed under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and the Kerala Public Ways (Restriction of Assemblies and Procession) Act, 2011, naming several high-ranking party officials as accused.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Covers the key details of the incident and the legal charges accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/muslim-youth-league-leaders-booked-over-rally-causing-traffic-obstruction-in-kochi/article71681658.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/kochi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kochi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
