       <h1>New Zealand Home ODI Streak Under Threat</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>New Zealand faces a challenge to their 11-match home ODI series winning streak as they prepare for the third ODI against India in Hamilton. The team has not lost a home series since 2019, but current conditions and performance concerns complicate their defense.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/new-zealand-home-odi-streak-under-threat.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Uncertainty surrounds the pitch due to wet weather, while the team manages player availability with Clarke added as cover. India plans to shift focus to Test preparations after this match, as New Zealand struggles with strike rotation and batting consistency.</p>
