     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-11-09 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>PPFAS Flexi Cap Fund Adjusts Portfolio with Netflix Buy and Meta Exit</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>In October 2026, the Parag Parikh Flexi Cap Fund added Netflix as a new investment, accounting for 3.06% of its assets, while completely exiting Meta Platforms. The fund also reduced its Microsoft holdings by 1.05% of its AUM, dropping from approximately 7.33 lakh shares to 4.21 lakh shares.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/ppfas-flexi-cap-fund-adjusts-portfolio-with-netflix-buy-and-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Domestically, the fund increased exposure to companies including DLF, Maruti Suzuki, and Mahindra &amp; Mahindra. As of October 31, 2026, the fund's total AUM reached approximately ₹1.47 lakh crore. While long-term rolling returns remain above the Nifty 500 TRI benchmark, the fund recorded a negative one-year lump-sum return of -5.48% for its direct plan.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Clear, data-dense summary that correctly attributes portfolio changes and performance figures from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/parag-parikh-flexi-cap-adds-netflix-exits-meta-what-changed-in-its-october-portfolio-check-latest-stock-picks-11794241378418.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
