     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-09 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Prasidh Krishna Reportedly Set for Delhi Capitals Move in IPL 2027 Trade</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#IPL</span></div>
       <p>Gujarat Titans pacer Prasidh Krishna is reportedly set to move to Delhi Capitals ahead of IPL 2027, with trade discussions between the two franchises currently underway. This development comes as the IPL trade and retention deadline approaches on November 17, 2026, leaving a narrow window to finalize any potential deal. Reports from Revsportz indicate the Titans are open to trading Krishna, with Ashutosh Sharma potentially moving from Delhi Capitals to Gujarat Titans as part of the exchange. As of November 8, 2026, neither franchise had issued an official confirmation of the trade.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/prasidh-krishna-reportedly-set-for-delhi-capitals-move-in-ip.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Prasidh Krishna was acquired by Gujarat Titans at the 2025 IPL mega auction for ₹9.5 crore, while Ashutosh Sharma was picked up by Delhi Capitals at the same auction for ₹3.80 crore. Krishna delivered a strong performance across his two seasons with the Titans in 2025 and 2026, collecting a combined 41 wickets from 27 matches. His 2025 campaign was particularly impressive, yielding 25 wickets at an average of 19.52, a performance that earned him the Purple Cap for that edition of the tournament.</p><p>In IPL 2026, Krishna secured 16 wickets from 12 matches, though his average increased to 25.44 and his economy rate stood at 10.44 across those appearances. Despite these slightly leaner numbers, his overall contribution underlined his value as a frontline pace option. Krishna's broader IPL career began with Kolkata Knight Riders in 2018, where he played for four seasons before joining Rajasthan Royals in 2022. He missed the 2023 and 2024 editions, returning with Gujarat Titans in 2025. Across 78 career IPL matches, he has taken 90 wickets at an average of 28.86, maintaining an economy rate under 9, with his 2025 Purple Cap win standing as a notable individual honor.</p><p>What to watch: Official trade confirmation before the November 17, 2026 deadline.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: A comprehensive summary of the reported trade talks, effectively using the provided statistics and career history.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/reports-gujarat-titans-pacer-prasidh-krishna-to-join-delhi-capitals-for-ipl-2027-1302/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
