     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-11-09 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ramayana – Part I Achieves Biggest Single-Day Global Collection of Rs. 151.77 Crores on Saturday, November 7</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Ramayana</span> <span>#Ranbir Kapoor</span> <span>#Yash</span></div>
       <p>The film *Ramayana – Part I*, starring Ranbir Kapoor and Yash, recorded its highest single-day collection at the worldwide box office on Saturday, November 7. The mythological epic grossed a remarkable Rs. 151.77 crores globally on its third day, successfully surpassing its opening-day figures and demonstrating a significant rebound after a decline on Friday.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/ramayana-part-i-achieves-biggest-single-day-global-collectio.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The theatrical journey for *Ramayana – Part I* commenced on Thursday, November 5, with initial worldwide collections standing at Rs. 125.52 crores gross. However, the film experienced a dip in collections on Friday, bringing in Rs. 100.38 crores. Saturday's performance marked a substantial turnaround, witnessing a massive 51.20% jump over Friday's earnings and adding Rs. 51.39 crores to its daily worldwide business.</p><p>Saturday's collection of Rs. 151.77 crores was approximately 20.91% higher than the opening-day figure from Thursday, solidifying it as the biggest single day in *Ramayana*'s theatrical run to date. This strong global performance on Saturday was driven by robust contributions from both the Indian and international markets.</p><p>Specifically, in India, *Ramayana* collected Rs. 67.80 crores nett, which translates to a gross collection of Rs. 80.71 crores. Overseas territories contributed an additional Rs. 71.05 crores gross, bringing the total reported worldwide collection for Saturday to Rs. 151.77 crores. International markets accounted for roughly 46.81% of Saturday’s worldwide gross, highlighting their substantial impact on the film's commercial momentum, with overseas business nearly matching the domestic gross.</p><p>The film's day-wise worldwide collections were Rs. 125.52 crores on Thursday (Day 1), Rs. 100.38 crores on Friday (Day 2), and Rs. 151.77 crores on Saturday (Day 3). Initial reports for Sunday (Day 4) indicated collections of Rs. 110.81 crores.</p><p>What to watch: The film's sustained performance in both domestic and international markets in the coming week.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article captures all quantitative data and context from the source material accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/saturday-creates-history-for-ranbir-kapoor-yash-starrer-ramayana-rs-151-77-cr-makes-it-the-films-biggest-day-globally/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
