       <h1>Sonia Gandhi Discusses Memoir and Political Legacy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Former Congress President Sonia Gandhi reflects on her life and political career in an interview with N. Ram regarding her upcoming memoir, 'Belonging: A Journey of Love.' She discusses her transition from her personal love story with Rajiv Gandhi to her long-term dedication to India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-09/sonia-gandhi-discusses-memoir-and-political-legacy.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In the interview, Gandhi also addresses the current political climate, criticizing the impact of twelve years of BJP-RSS governance on Indian democracy. She defends the Congress party’s ongoing efforts to maintain a level playing field in the national political arena, highlighting her perspective on the challenges facing the party and the country's democratic institutions.</p>
